{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The heavy-duty mounting tape felt useful because it could help me attach lightweight objects where my magnetic hooks cannot stick.",
    "The locking nuts connected to my recent screws and washers, while the caliper had a plausible use for checking hardware sizes, although neither was an immediate purchase."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Hose clamps and epoxy serve specific plumbing or repair needs that I have not shown; being hardware alone does not make them useful for my current tasks.",
    "Shopping bags, a large recycling bin and a fuel can did not connect to my recent fastening and mounting needs, and the bulk glue packs offered quantities I have no reason to buy."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat general workshop supplies as interchangeable with the small fasteners and mounting products I recently explored.",
    "My purchases of hardware assortments seemed to be taken as interest in bulk supplies generally, even though a useful assortment of sizes does not imply a need for many glue containers."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: my recent screw set uses metric M3, M4 and M5 sizes, so an SAE locking-nut assortment may not fit what I already have.",
    "I rarely act without a clear use: mounting tape offers a concrete extension of my magnetic hooks, while a large caliper would wait until I actually need precise measurements."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my fastening and mounting interests but stretched them into unrelated workshop needs without enough attention to compatibility or immediate usefulness."
}"}
